{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-160371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(6,-1),(-4,1),(3,5).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(-6,-1)$\n- $(4,-1)$\n- $(3,-5)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-160371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,1),(4,-1),(-3,-5).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-160371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "31c2feb4266eff72b427e01802c275f867994df67b826b638bbbd5094a9a83ca"} {"question" "q-160371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-160371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-160371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-160369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,5),(4,-3),(3,2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(2,5)$\n- $(-4,-3)$\n- $(-3,-2)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-160369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,-5),(-4,3),(-3,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-160369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "31c2feb4266eff72b427e01802c275f867994df67b826b638bbbd5094a9a83ca"} {"question" "q-160369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-160369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-160369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(4,1),(0,-3),(-1,3).$  Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(1,-3)$\n- $(-4,-1)$\n- $(0,3)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by the same angle. It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-4,-1),(0,3),(1,-3).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "31c2feb4266eff72b427e01802c275f867994df67b826b638bbbd5094a9a83ca"} {"question" "q-81815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-5,1),(0,-4),(3,5).$  Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians about the origin?\n\n- $(4,0)$\n- $(-3,-5)$\n- $(-1,5)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi },$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi }$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(5,-1),(0,4),(-3,-5).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "31c2feb4266eff72b427e01802c275f867994df67b826b638bbbd5094a9a83ca"} {"question" "q-81818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(4,4),(-3,-3),(-1,7).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(3,-3)$\n- $(-4,-4)$\n- $(1,-7)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-4,-4),(3,3),(1,-7).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "31c2feb4266eff72b427e01802c275f867994df67b826b638bbbd5094a9a83ca"} {"question" "q-81819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "7af97ae76e14aa75dd4f74f64cf75b0dd3c2edddec22686e25bc3214a14f8c19"} {"question" "q-81820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/assets/e6741c165a0f0f50bf932dd04c6d4c1157b4f70a8dc4c63efc5416b3883124bc.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector 